<%# The SPARC header — ONE definition, rendered by every layout (#974: two
    hand-copied headers had drifted, and the login page advertised less than
    the app). Since 1.18.0-rf it is the shell header (shared/_shell_header;
    #1297 retired the old layer menus, the sidebar and the #1042 two-tier
    collapse).

    The rules the old header taught, which the shell keeps:
      * navigation never moves: an entry is in the same place every time, and
        only whether it is SHOWN varies between viewers;
      * an entry is shown exactly when its screen admits the viewer — never a
        link that bounces to /login, never a hidden page that would open
        (SPARC_PUBLIC_CATALOGS opens the control library to anonymous viewers);
      * the header fits every width without a second row (#1042 needed two
        collapse tiers for the old menus; the shell's icons and tab bar do not). %>
<%= render "shared/shell_header" %>
